## What is new

- **A value computed by the program:** declared read only, `slide::readout("length", ...)`. The panel can show
  it (`controls=length`), and the slide with `<span data-demo-value="length">`.
- **The program tells the page:** when the length changes (a drag, another curve), `slide::notify()`; the page
  shows the new values and sends them to the slide, at most once a frame.
- **Picking:** at the click, `picking_spheres` finds the point under the mouse; while the button is down, the
  point follows the mouse in the plane facing the camera, and the camera stays still.

<div class="callout warn"><div class="callout-title">Lines of 1 pixel</div>

Most browsers draw WebGL lines one pixel wide, whatever `glLineWidth` asks: the curve is thin on a projector. A curve that must stay visible is better drawn as a tube, a mesh.

</div>

